{
  "schema": "research-public-artifact/v1",
  "concept": "Client-side operation timeout (CSOT)",
  "slug": "client-side-operation-timeout-csot",
  "canonical_concept_id": "concept:26539b50a936e6d753a695f3429db018d9ec8ab4680a997a28d20617390096c2",
  "canonical_artifact_sha256": "c81eb3bde0b625b5cf144a55f3a5f0de04b568367b8b0fd33d2031c3e855938a",
  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "clm:2c59ee3fb02ca2bef3fed9686be474440a287be2eb0ff47a7a3931ed112296ea",
      "text": "For ordinary non-tailable cursors, cursorLifetime is the default; iteration instead refreshes the budget for each cursor call. Pagination code must choose its intended scope. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/node/current/connect/connection-options/csot.md",
      "also": [
        "https://github.com/mongodb/node-mongodb-native/blob/main/EXPERIMENTAL_FEATURES.md"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:20c226fb56ebc7e05c1c420e2a42fa57af8129807c68953ed31b157d6c9fff5f",
        "ev:6ac1e800fdcdc5f5d73c41bc7b1a83ae54b68c5b15e944f2a99864ffb7c63b0c"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:648a6dbd2c8b18f463f77c229615d0626949335ebc08217508fcf847e326b052",
      "text": "An unset timeoutMS preserves legacy behavior; zero means an infinite operation budget, but serverSelectionTimeoutMS can still apply. Negative values are invalid. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/client-side-operations-timeout/client-side-operations-timeout.md",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "NOT-SAMPLED",
      "evidence_ids": []
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:aa3895e8e055ddaae496cc26965f3f01edcb86a04fb96d8c40e3771a49173fc0",
      "text": "When timeoutMS is set, it overrides socketTimeoutMS, waitQueueTimeoutMS, wTimeoutMS, maxTimeMS, and maxCommitTimeMS. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/node/current/connect/connection-options/csot.md",
      "also": [
        "https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/client-side-operations-timeout/client-side-operations-timeout.md"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:82521df032d98c0b2adcb92c17e15187bce0e8241197dbe8ec8bf539188308c9"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:9dd13abedc884c3fae292d44ba0994e2ec33bac6e695593ecc5cc8335f7c6ba2",
      "text": "ErrLookup reproduces Node.js ConnectionPool.checkOut code that wraps WaitQueueTimeoutError in MongoOperationTimeoutError with the message \"Timed out during connection checkout\" when CSOT is enabled. This identifies pool waiting as a timeout stage before query execution. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-08-11)",
      "source_url": "https://errors.standardbeagle.com/mongodb/node-mongodb-native/timed-out-during-connection-checkout/",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:2a901234556bf4770b1b8015a192069dd9ddc7d3facae05dec26fb7e5d8575f4",
        "ev:45be2a56a0ae819fd2a4bfcc8275aab8399330670ef6b9225e7d1a283926df93"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:5adf970e276f632a6cebea796c80ecac5eb1c21b098d4f4b47d5ad9510116d09",
      "text": "Under the specification, a non-tailable cursor may return already-buffered documents after its lifetime budget expires; timeout is raised when another getMore is required. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/client-side-operations-timeout/client-side-operations-timeout.md",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:339368b93987d0149bdafcff2b7b19f4cadc126ae4e1cf44989d21ffa403c467"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:ac12c8ef3f97df215b4c585eb0adfd2ef2cae5d8333db97fb579ba7efcb862b4",
      "text": "The specification deducts minimum network RTT when deriving server maxTimeMS. Insufficient remaining time can cause rejection before sending the command. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/client-side-operations-timeout/client-side-operations-timeout.md",
      "also": [
        "https://pymongo.readthedocs.io/en/4.11.2/examples/timeouts.html"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:18b303ae4072336326859c0805a20d2827cc16d42c29c16bafaae5f61e892542"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:f11ce31121200de9199d28035e3e9192dda1f9997593069ec06679bed9fb9cd9",
      "text": "The independent go-dto/go-common v0.2.0 wrapper documents Config.Timeout as CSOT used when the operation context has no deadline, with zero meaning none. This is wrapper-specific evidence, not a universal cross-driver precedence rule. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/go-dto/go-common@v0.2.0/database/mongodb",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:0dec6a2d4655f15e93884fe20227fd27a6982b764d97f3f2254fd22b0aa8f9de",
        "ev:78a4bfd42584fe4e2a3e857e8dea488a30d2e806784d04211d3822e0c3f781b5",
        "ev:94fe97b0cf58911852662046382b2097f1cfc9fb7ff624cbfebabd390666ccc7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:6c2217782a7df5a9db2e908441ac7a7b2d3f223b4fde859709aff47938bb139c",
      "text": "Configure a client default and override timeoutMS for individual operations; an override inside a withTransaction callback using its timed session is invalid. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/node/current/connect/connection-options/csot.md",
      "also": [
        "https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/client-side-operations-timeout/client-side-operations-timeout.md"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:88d91f6f48f94da0f762a1295804089f091667ec47a3b968bc4fb022b75f44c6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:dd26cd9bb637eda9e49733404680c27660dc17655ec5ba9d49fadbe1a3ccaf07",
      "text": "MongoDB documented a CSOT failure mode where latency spikes caused socket timeouts, connection churn, and further server load. DRIVERS-2884 describes pending-response reuse as a proposed mitigation, not a universal shipped guarantee. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-09-23)",
      "source_url": "https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/DRIVERS-2884",
      "also": [
        "https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/client-side-operations-timeout/client-side-operations-timeout.md"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:cfce3d747cc18cb223b2b5ed34e9c99822b8cb73e1dc3ff086240eeb56874672",
        "ev:fd964a4fadaa9a9c5282498b9447b845f39c2d7e005b56e5bad885cf95c363d5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:e625271e8c6634c368096aa1dbf105437f67a69f51507f26f7379517a65abcc4",
      "text": "PyMongo 4.11.2 documents pymongo.timeout(seconds) as a deadline for all driver operations in its block. Nested blocks may shorten but cannot extend the outer deadline; the block overrides client timeoutMS. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pymongo.readthedocs.io/en/4.11.2/examples/timeouts.html",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:260fa007bf0ed2c95ee61e32c795b5a3886312095cda8a02232f4c1f4ec37e45"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:381c8fe26091c220681138b51e78e30d20e4b1a66b259d80ced17bb6c57e9ddf",
      "text": "The Node.js guide and experimental-features file both mark CSOT experimental; validate behavior against the deployed driver rather than assuming that an accepted specification means a stable implementation. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/node/current/connect/connection-options/csot.md",
      "also": [
        "https://github.com/mongodb/node-mongodb-native/blob/main/EXPERIMENTAL_FEATURES.md"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:38c065990e3ea14a4e8a76e5b08df76314ec2e914119119599922047588a3679",
        "ev:390282a420bfb87922808ec22155b407e751772ad5561c76eff3f7e5c1fd4b28",
        "ev:3a37d70d802653bf63f7c33ee21e7b1fbe802efdfcfc009e3cd93d9d0c2a1f44"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:00b81c1ad2c8c1f3895c2011317a97781dfab631cda8eb03d5b6b91cf5634481",
      "text": "CSOT uses timeoutMS as a shared operation budget covering server selection, connection checkout and server execution; it is a best-effort deadline. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/client-side-operations-timeout/client-side-operations-timeout.md",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/node/current/connect/connection-options/csot.md"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:2044be4714dc2b401cd9a69567a91f4c26186a240f9855b5d0cd19e6328a81c5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:fbacbdaffd57f61c814484261a424e1a5f79c39d0adfb39c0a2c9f8a4bd66681",
      "text": "Cursor cleanup gets a refreshed timeout for killCursors, so cleanup can extend beyond the original cursor budget. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/node/current/connect/connection-options/csot.md",
      "also": [
        "https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/client-side-operations-timeout/client-side-operations-timeout.md"
      ],
      "validation_status": "NOT-SAMPLED",
      "evidence_ids": []
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:708cd2bdf7bb47f680bc670c0c741b392defbdd96a276bb90f08c400bf8fa06b",
      "text": "The specification defines a best-effort deadline: transaction-abort cleanup can make withTransaction take up to twice timeoutMS. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/client-side-operations-timeout/client-side-operations-timeout.md",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:afa052ef79f8c1385b9bd0514e9e791b691fbfe5e45d3f9590ae07cc9519afb8",
        "ev:fb5225ab63a8e49f1963694607e296e3deecfd68534e87d305ef69ad801a7220"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:83b2daf160ed085920c76c443647a9278d769d7f6034320dbed4e25af92c22ac",
      "text": "The specification retains serverSelectionTimeoutMS and connectTimeoutMS; timeoutMS=0 does not eliminate every other timeout. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/client-side-operations-timeout/client-side-operations-timeout.md",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:09ab7f4f1a506ead3bb37bab889cd46596fa368f33367052f913fd98f74d90e9",
        "ev:131c8a63cc6c4ec139573e01cc6f084c9fe60c6df6a6a3bb8a131adc266e9e18"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:6bdcaf383a34fc9d77455d725a1e9abac80d1e7e7e7295d8ee84c4ee52f68649",
      "text": "Eligible retries consume the same timeoutMS budget, and a multi-batch bulk write shares one budget across its batches. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/client-side-operations-timeout/client-side-operations-timeout.md",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:beb55e54232b4daad6650b49827aa89849e781648ee8b259063d38ab08b2b15e"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:a910dfedc2ee1eef0aea006756a255fd5ecde85fa05cdb7b8045ed7e3d20cf8c",
      "text": "Spring Data issue 5003 requested per-operation CSOT overrides; a June 16, 2025 contributor comment suggested waiting until the driver feature ceased being experimental. This establishes integration demand, not completed framework support. (low confidence) (verified as of 2025-06-16)",
      "source_url": "https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-data-mongodb/issues/5003",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:98ba0e200e7f43f1214915e38ed2675dc9a845a5fc2f074edc2de333e763570d"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:47ae3f7707fad4a932c50c5b1fd4ecf57fb4c7773a0c8d771d1d07b045031220",
      "text": "In Node.js, timeoutMS overrides socketTimeoutMS, waitQueueTimeoutMS, wTimeoutMS, maxTimeMS and maxCommitTimeMS. Ordinary per-operation overrides can customize a client-level budget. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/node/current/connect/connection-options/csot.md",
      "also": [
        "https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/client-side-operations-timeout/client-side-operations-timeout.md"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:fce4a2b70439ea1d88fb867231d72a7f7cbf4b57b07576d3383dc2274ab0de30"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:e5984bcffc219d7f99447e003322a744a0f9bc3ada0a63862b7d5c62e6bc2ae8",
      "text": "Node.js documents CSOT as experimental. Its experimental-features policy permits behavior and TypeScript compatibility changes even in patch and minor releases. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/node/current/connect/connection-options/csot.md",
      "also": [
        "https://github.com/mongodb/node-mongodb-native/blob/main/EXPERIMENTAL_FEATURES.md"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:390282a420bfb87922808ec22155b407e751772ad5561c76eff3f7e5c1fd4b28",
        "ev:3a37d70d802653bf63f7c33ee21e7b1fbe802efdfcfc009e3cd93d9d0c2a1f44"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:8cdabf329087167fbe240abcc7c8269e0dbd595d5d8d639a1ba2642d05902678",
      "text": "Node.js cursors support cursorLifetime and iteration timeout modes. Non-tailable cursors default to cursorLifetime; tailable cursors default to iteration, which budgets each next() call. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/node-mongodb-native/blob/main/EXPERIMENTAL_FEATURES.md",
      "also": [
        "https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/client-side-operations-timeout/client-side-operations-timeout.md"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:936330b37c33a005a330571e97c0c0204c789b69300e1c25d31e7d0910ec8511"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:31dc9c571c67087b202935ac4ed7b22f10a8a147d594f6d07c797f6df9d79d51",
      "text": "Node.js disallows an operation-level timeoutMS override within the explicit session passed to a withTransaction() callback. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/node/current/connect/connection-options/csot.md",
      "also": [
        "https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/client-side-operations-timeout/client-side-operations-timeout.md"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:93c863a107938ef6473381ca10498bfc8a645f2150cb0f17029f676f2ca29f43",
        "ev:c71538a30ba969bd862d13762a377424bb32665a1ea054de2e2c1c16df236382"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:949eb587f30e13a4df6b7d47e9c8f5179024e4fa19b600b3b2a331ed95798391",
      "text": "A PyMongo timeout does not prove that a write had no effect: its documentation warns that a server-cancelled operation may have partially completed. PyMongoError.timeout identifies timeout-related failures. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pymongo.readthedocs.io/en/4.11.2/examples/timeouts.html",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "NOT-SAMPLED",
      "evidence_ids": []
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:a13220c2a1172a296b9b5c8f3c3126bcb7611b6841d43d87349846416ffff865",
      "text": "Spring Data MongoDB issue #5003, opened June 15, 2025, requests per-operation timeoutMS overrides; the request demonstrates that driver functionality and framework-level configuration are separate integration concerns. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-data-mongodb/issues/5003",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:4220b8a6969372f9c83b4b87756211942fea756042fea53fc40c2156364ea2e6"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "projection_sha256": "6ce7ee62280526c0d30e05f7e2c17cb0db809dc64b57b68e39bcda899548a318"
}
